# WHITEWATCH / War Map — optional environment variables.
# The feature works with none of these set: news comes from free public RSS,
# conflict/country-threat data comes from the curated JSON in lib/whitewatch-data/,
# and predictions show clearly-labeled placeholder text. Add keys below to
# upgrade each piece to a live source. Same variable names work locally
# (.env.local, gitignored by Next.js by default) and in Vercel's
# Project Settings -> Environment Variables.

# Anthropic API key — enables live AI-generated 7-day outlooks on the
# Predictions tab instead of placeholder text. Get one at https://console.anthropic.com
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Mapbox token — not required for the map itself (MapLibre GL + free raster
# basemaps are used, no Mapbox account needed). Only set this if you later
# want to switch to Mapbox-hosted vector tiles/styles instead of the free
# CARTO/Esri raster basemaps already wired up. Get one at https://account.mapbox.com
MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# NewsAPI.org key — optional additional news source alongside the free RSS
# feeds already wired up (BBC, Al Jazeera, NYT, Guardian, DW, Reuters).
# Not currently consumed by /api/whitewatch/news — reserved for a future
# upgrade. Get one at https://newsapi.org
NEWSAPI_KEY=

# ACLED (Armed Conflict Location & Event Data) credentials — swaps the
# curated lib/whitewatch-data/conflicts.json for a live ACLED pull once
# wired up in app/api/whitewatch/conflicts/route.js. Not yet consumed —
# reserved for a future upgrade. Register at https://acleddata.com/register
ACLED_API_KEY=
ACLED_EMAIL=

# X (formerly Twitter) API v2 bearer token — enables the X panel on the
# Live tab. IMPORTANT: X's free API tier does not include search access —
# you need a paid Basic tier (or higher) developer account to get a token
# that works here. Apply at https://developer.x.com. Without this set, the
# X panel just shows an explanatory placeholder — nothing breaks.
X_BEARER_TOKEN=

# NASA FIRMS (Fire Information for Resource Management System) MAP_KEY —
# enables the "Active fires (FIRMS)" layer on the War Map (near-real-time
# thermal-anomaly/fire detections worldwide). Free, instant signup (no
# approval wait) at https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/area/ — click
# "Get MAP_KEY". Without this set, the layer's toggle shows a note instead
# of data — nothing breaks.
FIRMS_MAP_KEY=

# FRED (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis) API key — enables the
# Commodities ticker on the Dashboard tab (WTI crude, Brent crude, Henry
# Hub natural gas). Free, instant signup at
# https://fredaccount.stlouisfed.org/apikeys. Without this set, the
# Dashboard just shows the ticker as "Not connected" — nothing breaks.
FRED_API_KEY=

# Hugging Face API token — enables REAL FinBERT (ProsusAI/finbert)
# financial-news sentiment scoring on the Ticker Hub's "News sentiment"
# panel (src/app/api/models/sentiment/route.ts). Without this set, every
# headline is honestly labeled "sentiment scoring unavailable" — no
# fabricated or keyword-guessed score is shown in its place.
#
# How to get one, and what it costs (verified 2026-09-13 — see
# src/lib/sentiment/finbert.ts for the full research writeup):
#   1. Create a free account at https://huggingface.co/join (no payment
#      method required to sign up).
#   2. Create a token at https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens/new with
#      the "Make calls to Inference Providers" permission.
#   3. Paste it below.
# Every account — including a brand-new free one — gets a small monthly
# inference credit (documented by Hugging Face as $0.10/month as of this
# writing, "subject to change") that pays for calls to ProsusAI/finbert (a
# small, cheap-to-run CPU model) at Hugging Face's own metered rate. This is
# NOT an unlimited free tier — once the monthly credit is used up, calls
# fail cleanly with HTTP 402 (Payment Required) rather than silently
# degrading or auto-charging; this app's fallback for an individual failed
# call is a clearly-labeled cruder keyword heuristic, never a re-labeled
# real score. Not independently load-tested from this codebase — this
# sandbox has no outbound network access to actually call the endpoint; see
# finbert.ts for exactly what was and wasn't verified.
HF_API_KEY=

# Tradier SANDBOX API token — enables the "Options market — implied move"
# panel on the Ticker Hub (real options chain + greeks/IV, courtesy of
# ORATS, for the nearest standard-monthly expiration). Free developer
# signup, NO funded brokerage account required: sign up at
# https://developer.tradier.com/user/sign_up (or tradier.com generally),
# then generate a "Sandbox" token (not a production one) at
# https://web.tradier.com/user/api. IMPORTANT limitations, straight from
# Tradier's own docs (docs.tradier.com/docs/faq, docs.tradier.com/docs/
# rate-limiting) — quote these accurately if you ever explain this feature
# to a member: sandbox market data is delayed the "industry standard
# 15-minutes", greeks/IV can lag up to another hour on top of that (ORATS
# recomputes hourly), the sandbox rate limit is 60 requests/minute for
# market-data endpoints, and "Unless you are a Tradier Partner, Tradier
# APIs are entitled for personal use only" — this data must stay inside the
# fund's own platform, never redistributed or resold. Without this set, the
# panel shows a clear "not configured" state — nothing breaks, and nothing
# fabricated is shown in its place.
TRADIER_API_KEY=

# SEC EDGAR operator contact — the Ticker Hub's "Insider activity
# (WW-Insider)" panel (src/app/api/models/insider/route.ts, backed by
# src/lib/whitewatch-data/edgar-sources.js) pulls live SEC Form 4
# insider-transaction filings from data.sec.gov / www.sec.gov. There is NO
# API key for this — SEC EDGAR is entirely free and keyless — but SEC's own
# fair-access policy (verified 2026-09-13 at
# https://www.sec.gov/os/accessing-edgar-data) requires every request to
# carry a descriptive User-Agent identifying the calling application AND a
# real contact, e.g. SEC's own example "Sample Company Name
# AdminContact@<sample company domain>.com", plus a courtesy 10 requests/
# second rate limit (already respected by this route's per-ticker cache and
# per-request fetch cap — see edgar-sources.js). Without this set, requests
# still go out (identified as "WhiteWaterCapitalInsiderBot/1.0" with a link
# back to this repo's deployment) — set it to the desk's real operational
# contact before relying on this in production, per SEC's policy.
SEC_EDGAR_CONTACT=

# --- Nothing to set for these — listed here so you know they're live ---
# Global Indicators tab (energy use, electricity access, freshwater
# withdrawal, GDP growth, inflation, refugee/IDP figures per country) pulls
# live from three merged sources: the World Bank Open Data API
# (api.worldbank.org), the IMF DataMapper API (imf.org/external/datamapper),
# and the UNHCR Refugee Statistics API (api.unhcr.org) — all public, no
# key, no signup.
# Power Plants list pulls live from the Global Power Plant Database (World
# Resources Institute, CC BY 4.0) — public CSV on GitHub, no key.
# Mines/Ports/Smelters/Refineries/Dams layers pull live from three merged
# sources: Wikidata's public SPARQL query service (query.wikidata.org),
# OpenStreetMap's Overpass API (overpass-api.de), and USGS MRDS (mines
# only, mrdata.usgs.gov) — no key, no signup for any of them.
# Intel Feed also pulls live from GDELT's DOC 2.0 API
# (api.gdeltproject.org) alongside the curated RSS feeds — public, no key.
# Earthquakes layer on the War Map pulls live from the USGS Earthquake
# Hazards Program's GeoJSON feed (earthquake.usgs.gov) — public, no key,
# updates every minute.
# Live tab's Bloomberg panel embeds Bloomberg Originals' own free public
# YouTube livestream — no key, and it's Bloomberg's own sanctioned stream,
# not a paywalled or scraped source.
